From ea02fb0f0165d44b0b64f6608eadb0d9d493cdea Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Akif-b-Atif <akif.b.atif@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 15:29:44 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix @-mention/identity resolution and related parsing bugs

- Resolve contact-name @mentions (wrapped in U+2068/U+2069 isolates), not
  just @<digits>, so the same message exported from two phones normalizes
  identically and merges as a duplicate
- Stop isolate-wrapped tags leaking names into phrase/word stats and
  mention counts (the bogus top 'Akif Bin Atif' phrase)
- Canonical names are implicit aliases; alias keys ignore case, emoji
  variation selectors, NFKC form and the '~ ' non-contact prefix; report
  alias conflicts instead of silently overwriting
- Treat colon-containing event lines as system events; keep blank lines
  inside multi-paragraph messages
- Analyzer: [SYSTEM] lines never become senders, sender-length cap raised,
  stable timestamp sort, Unicode-aware word tokenizer, exact-name mention
  matches beat first-name matches, saner mention boundaries
- Nickname parts that are ordinary words no longer become stopwords
- normalize_export saves identities after every answer; shared
  assign_alias; warn on unresolved mentions and ambiguous date order
- Add regression tests
